WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
SpaceX thrusters give the Tesla Roadster aerial flight and roll capability ahead of 2028 production. This is SpaceX Daily Episode 132. A tent at McGregor, long rumored to hold starship hardware is where the demo vehicle system was revealed, according to Paul Tan. The car uses cold gas reaction control system, or RCS, thrusters first built for SpaceX spacecraft. Those units share the same cold gas architecture flown on dragon and on early starship attitude control.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.240
control. The claims sprint is 0-96 kilometers per hour in 0.81 seconds. The work is a direct

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:41.480
hardware transfer from orbital vehicles to a terrestrial performance demonstration.

00:00:42.393 --> 00:00:47.013
Reddit users looking at that same McGregor hardware noted that cold gas systems need

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:51.713
only low mass flow, which makes them practical on a lightweight demonstration vehicle.

00:00:52.593 --> 00:01:00.233
Commenters also speculated about scaling that thruster family later to crude vehicles. Project

00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:05.473
effort, aiming to fold national capabilities into one launch and satellite services provider,

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:10.753
trading key reports. The project would put multiple national pads and factories under

00:01:10.753 --> 00:01:16.153
a single operator. Early planning documents emphasize reuse goals similar to those Falcon

00:01:16.153 --> 00:01:21.073
9 and New Glenn have already shown. Analysts question whether it can match SpaceX

00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:26.413
cadence or pricing given different capital and manufacturing approaches. European launch

00:01:26.413 --> 00:01:30.833
A bunch of analysts on X compared Bromo's planned factory scale against Rocket Lab's

00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:36.233
neutron timeline, and pointed to Blue Origin's existing Artemis contracts as a capital buffer.

00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:41.693
They also noted that monthly cadence targets for New Glenn would still lag Starship's projected

00:01:41.693 --> 00:01:43.953
flight rate even after a return to flight.

00:01:44.853 --> 00:01:49.433
Commenters highlighted government funding models versus SpaceX's private capital approach.

00:01:50.371 --> 00:01:56.411
Starlink satellite 31,069 returned to its target altitude after a swing and has held

00:01:56.411 --> 00:02:02.691
position since. Keep track reported as routine consolation monitoring. The 11 kilometer deviation

00:02:02.691 --> 00:02:07.531
occurred during elevated solar activity that increased atmospheric drag on lower orbits.

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:13.371
Onboard propulsion restored the 490 kilometer altitude without interrupting service links.

00:02:14.539 --> 00:02:19.519
SpaceX's AI policy head is scheduled to testify Friday before the New York City Council.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:25.539
Market screener reports. The testimony will address the council's ongoing probe into AI safety

00:02:25.539 --> 00:02:30.679
standards in oversight. The hearing is the first scheduled public regulatory engagement by a

00:02:30.679 --> 00:02:35.979
SpaceX policy lead on standards that could affect both ground-based and orbital compute systems.

00:02:36.639 --> 00:02:41.299
City officials have framed the session as part of a broader review of AI deployment risks

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:47.446
in municipal and commercial contexts. The original Tesla Roadster remains on an elliptical path

00:02:47.446 --> 00:02:53.746
between Earth and Mars. Elon Musk confirmed on X. The car went up on a Falcon Heavy in 2018

00:02:53.746 --> 00:02:57.146
and has seen no reported change to its trajectory or condition.

00:02:57.906 --> 00:03:00.546
Amateur astronomers have tracked its reflective surfaces

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.286
and orbital elements for years.

00:03:02.906 --> 00:03:05.386
Elon Musk also said execution outweighs

00:03:05.386 --> 00:03:07.386
available capital in rocket development,

00:03:07.906 --> 00:03:11.106
posting on X in reply to a discussion of resource allocation

00:03:11.106 --> 00:03:12.546
versus delivery speed.

00:03:13.086 --> 00:03:16.566
He has used similar phrasing in prior updates on starship timelines,

00:03:17.086 --> 00:03:19.586
stressing manufacturing throughput and test cadence

00:03:19.586 --> 00:03:20.986
over extra funding rounds.

00:03:20.986 --> 00:03:25.839
problems. In a second exchange the same day, Musk replied, we can do better to feedback

00:03:25.839 --> 00:03:31.319
on recent operations. The brief exchange referenced unspecified performance areas without

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:35.839
naming programs, and followed multiple operational updates posted that day.

00:03:36.699 --> 00:03:40.819
Observers read the reply as an acknowledgement that incremental improvements are still needed

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:46.169
across launch and satellite fleets. Worth keeping an eye on Project Bromo's integration

00:03:46.169 --> 00:03:51.169
challenges across countries, which analysts say could slow any combined European operator

00:03:51.169 --> 00:03:53.929
even with new Glenn already demonstrating reuse.

00:03:54.509 --> 00:03:59.809
Success would still require engine production rates that have historically lagged US commercial timelines.

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:05.009
Differing national procurement rules are an additional hurdle that could extend development cycles.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.960
Carbon fiber tanks sit at the engineering angle this week.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.100
Because a kilogram saved in the wall is a kilogram you can sell as payload.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.000
A trade NASA space flights reporting on neutron keeps forcing back onto the table.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.800
A rocket tank is a pressure vessel, and the hoop stress in the wall is pressure times

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.260
radius divided by thickness.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.120
Longitudinal stress is half that, so the cylinder wants fibers mostly around the hoop, while

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.960
the domes want pads that run toward the polar bosses.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:38.600
Double the diameter, and for the same pressure, you need roughly twice the wall thickness, so

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.600
dry mass climbs unless strength to weight climbs with it.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:47.240
High-grade fiber beats aluminium and steel on tensile strength per kilogram, which is the

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.540
The entire reason a composite tank looks good on a mass budget.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:54.700
Alluminium sits around 2.7 grams per cubic centimeter.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.640
Accured carbon fiber laminate is on the order of 1.6.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:05.100
Fiber tensile strength typically lands in the 3-7 gigapascal range, versus a few hundred

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.020
megapascals for common aluminium tank alloys.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.000
Those raw inputs are the magic wand number.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.740
Fiber plus resin plus heat and pressure in a cure cycle.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:20.700
The finished tank costs many times that, an idiot index that an aerospace composites often

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:26.740
lands on the order of 10-50, because autoclaves, scrap, inspection, and rejected plies eat

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.260
the savings.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:33.160
What actually decides whether mass savings reach orbit is fiber volume fraction, the share

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.580
of the laminate that is fiber rather than resin.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.020
Too high and the part will not consolidate without voids.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.440
Too low and extra resin adds weight and cuts stiffness.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.620
A typical shop target sits around 60% fiber by volume.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.520
A back-of-envelope figure chased with lay-up tension and resin flow.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.880
A 1% void fraction is not a cosmetic flaw.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.000
It is a stress razor, and under cyclic pressure it becomes a crack starter.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:04.740
Automated placement machines set toes on program paths, so the wall can take ascent loads, internal

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:08.220
pressure, and the buckling and shear of a reusable first stage.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.040
Reuse is the extra problem metal tanks already understand.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:17.580
Landing and boost back put the skin in compression, so buckling stiffness matters as much as

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.160
burst strength.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:23.720
Higher modulus grades help that buckling resistance, yet they cost more and snap more

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:27.320
easily and handling, so a drop toe can scrap a whole panel.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:32.820
Rocket Labs' neutron delay shows how the same material that worked on electron misbehaves

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:36.720
when the tank gets wider and longer on a medium lift first stage.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:42.120
Geodesic paths that sat nicely on a small dome start bridging and wrinkling on a large

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:42.400
one.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:47.700
Tension that was fine at electron scale can starve or flood the resonant neutron scale.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:54.900
Pure temperature and pressure, often in the 120-180 degree Celsius band for epoxies, set

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.400
interlaminor shear strength.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:01.780
Scale the geometry and those profiles stop being interchangeable because the thermal mass

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.960
of a big tool soaks heat at a different rate than a small one.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:10.920
Criogenic propellant adds another cut, resin and fiber shrink at different rates and repeated

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:16.060
cold soaks can microcrack the matrix even when room temperature coupons looked clean.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:21.280
Metal polar bosses still have to meet the composite, and that joint is where leak paths

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.560
hide if the ply drop-offs are sloppy.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.720
Post-cure inspection, ultrasound or thermography, is the step that decides whether a tank is

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:35.540
flight hardware or scrap. And it is also where the idiot index quietly grows. Handlayup

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:40.560
still handles awkward shapes, but it injects variability that automation is built to kill.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:45.160
Fiber orientation you can see during placement is the directional strength map,

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:50.460
and it has to balance hoop tension against sheer unique to a booster that flies more than once.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:56.940
Close the process window on tension, flow, cure, and inspection, and the mass saving show up as

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:01.640
load, miss it, and the extra safety margin eats every kilogram you thought you had bought.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:06.800
On the tape, SPCX finished slightly higher, up a fraction of a percent.

